          "source": "NCERT Exemplar",
          "question": "There are two values of $a$ which make the determinant $\\Delta = \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & a & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2a \\end{vmatrix} = 86$. The sum of these two values is:",
          "options": [
            "$4$",
            "$5$",
            "$-4$",
            "$9$"
          ],
          "solution": {
            "answer": "(C) $-4$",
            "concept": "Expand a $3 \\times 3$ determinant along a row: $\\Delta = a_{11}A_{11} + a_{12}A_{12} + a_{13}A_{13}$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Expand along $R_1$.",
                "math": "\\Delta = 1(2a^2 + 4) + 2(4a - 0) + 5(8 - 0) = 2a^2 + 8a + 44"
              },
              {
                "do": "Put $\\Delta = 86$.",
                "math": "2a^2 + 8a - 42 = 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; a^2 + 4a - 21 = 0"
              },
              {
                "do": "Factorise.",
                "math": "(a + 7)(a - 3) = 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; a = -7 \\text{ or } a = 3"
              },
              {
                "do": "Add the two values.",
                "math": "-7 + 3 = -4",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Hence option (C)."
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Taking $-2$ in place of $+2$ for the middle term: the sign pattern gives $-(-2)(4a) = +8a$."
          }
        },
