          "type": "long",
          "source": "PYQ-style",
          "question": "A school wants to award its students for the values of Honesty, Regularity and Hard work with a total cash award of ₹6,000. Three times the award money for Hard work added to that given for Honesty amounts to ₹11,000. The award money given for Honesty and Hard work together is double the one given for Regularity. Represent the situation algebraically and find the award money for each value, using the matrix method.",
          "solution": {
            "answer": "Honesty ₹500, Regularity ₹2,000, Hard work ₹3,500",
            "concept": "$AX = B \\Rightarrow X = A^{-1}B$, where $A^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{|A|}\\,\\text{adj}\\,A$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Let the awards for Honesty, Regularity, Hard work be ₹$x$, ₹$y$, ₹$z$.",
                "math": "x + y + z = 6000,\\quad x + 3z = 11000,\\quad x - 2y + z = 0",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Write as $AX = B$.",
                "math": "\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 6000 \\\\ 11000 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix}"
              },
              {
                "do": "Find $|A|$ by expanding along $R_1$.",
                "math": "|A| = 1(0 + 6) - 1(1 - 3) + 1(-2 - 0) = 6 \\ne 0",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Cofactors of row 1.",
                "math": "A_{11} = 6,\\quad A_{12} = 2,\\quad A_{13} = -2"
              },
              {
                "do": "Cofactors of row 2.",
                "math": "A_{21} = -3,\\quad A_{22} = 0,\\quad A_{23} = 3"
              },
              {
                "do": "Cofactors of row 3.",
                "math": "A_{31} = 3,\\quad A_{32} = -2,\\quad A_{33} = -1",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "$\\text{adj}\\,A$ is the transpose of the cofactor matrix.",
                "math": "\\text{adj}\\,A = \\begin{bmatrix} 6 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Write $A^{-1}$.",
                "math": "A^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix} 6 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Find $X = A^{-1}B$.",
                "math": "X = \\dfrac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix} 36000 - 33000 + 0 \\\\ 12000 + 0 - 0 \\\\ -12000 + 33000 - 0 \\end{bmatrix} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix} 3000 \\\\ 12000 \\\\ 21000 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 500 \\\\ 2000 \\\\ 3500 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Hence Honesty ₹500, Regularity ₹2,000 and Hard work ₹3,500.",
                "marks": 0.5
              }
            ],
            "mistake": "Writing the third condition as $2(x + z) = y$; it is $x + z = 2y$."
          }
