          "source": "CBSE 2025",
          "question": "Given $A = \\begin{bmatrix} -4 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}$ and $B = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}$, find $AB$. Hence, solve the system of linear equations: $x - y + z = 4$, $x - 2y - 2z = 9$, $2x + y + 3z = 1$.",
          "solution": {
            "answer": "$AB = 8I$; $x = 3$, $y = -2$, $z = -1$",
            "concept": "If $AB = kI$ with $k \\ne 0$, then $B^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{k}A$.",
            "steps": [
              {
                "do": "Row 1 of $AB$.",
                "math": "(-4 + 4 + 8,\\ 4 - 8 + 4,\\ -4 - 8 + 12) = (8,\\ 0,\\ 0)",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Row 2 of $AB$.",
                "math": "(-7 + 1 + 6,\\ 7 - 2 + 3,\\ -7 - 2 + 9) = (0,\\ 8,\\ 0)",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Row 3 of $AB$.",
                "math": "(5 - 3 - 2,\\ -5 + 6 - 1,\\ 5 + 6 - 3) = (0,\\ 0,\\ 8)",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "So $AB$ is $8$ times the identity.",
                "math": "AB = \\begin{bmatrix} 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 \\end{bmatrix} = 8I",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "The system has coefficient matrix $B$: $BX = C$.",
                "math": "\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "From $AB = 8I$: $\\left(\\tfrac{1}{8}A\\right)B = I$.",
                "math": "B^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{8}A",
                "marks": 1
              },
              {
                "do": "Find $X = B^{-1}C$.",
                "math": "X = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix} -4 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -1 \\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix} 4 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 1 \\end{bmatrix} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix} -16 + 36 + 4 \\\\ -28 + 9 + 3 \\\\ 20 - 27 - 1 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Simplify.",
                "math": "X = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix} 24 \\\\ -16 \\\\ -8 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\end{bmatrix}",
                "marks": 0.5
              },
              {
                "do": "Hence $x = 3$, $y = -2$, $z = -1$.",
                "marks": 0.5
              }
